description:
Change one of the following settings: accent color, appearance (light/dark mode), or personality. Use get_user_settings to see the option enums available before changing. If it's ambiguous what new setting the user wants, clarify (usually by providing them information about the options available) before changing their settings. Be sure to tell them what the 'official' name is of the new setting option set so they know what you changed. You may ONLY set_settings to allowed values, there are NO OTHER valid options available.

```ts
user_settings__set_setting(args: 
 | {
setting_name: "accent_color",
// Accent color. Availability varies by plan and feature rollout; get_user_settings returns the exact options for this user.
setting_value: "default" | "blue" | "green" | "yellow" | "pink" | "orange" | "red" | "purple" | "black" | "gray",
}
 | { setting_name: "appearance", setting_value: "system" | "light" | "dark" }
 | {
setting_name: "personality",
// Personality name. Canonical values are: default, professional, listener, coach, creative, robot, nerd, cynic, sidekick. The exact available display names are returned by get_user_settings.
setting_value: string,
}
): Promise<{ setting_name: string, old_value: string | null, new_value: string }>;
```

