Read a known file or range from the current Project context, including Project-backed files returned with source_kind='project'. Pass every read request under the required top-level `read` wrapper with a `ref_id`, for example {"read":[{"ref_id":"turn1file0"}]}. Use files.search for broad retrieval and files.find for exact text before expanding with files.read.

For visual questions, inspect relevant images before answering. When `image()` is available, emit relevant images and citations from the result `r` in the same `functions.exec` call as retrieval:
```js
for (const result of r.results ?? []) {
  for (const part of result.content ?? []) {
    if (typeof part === "string") {
      text(part);
    } else if (part?.content_type === "image_asset_pointer" && part.image_url) {
      image(part); text(part.citation_marker);
    }
  }
}
```
`text(...)` alone does not display images.

